---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
const base=import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/,'');
const faq=[
 ['Can I use two Claude Desktop accounts on one Windows PC?','Yes. Hatrack opens each profile as its own Claude Desktop instance with a separate data folder, so you sign in to each one separately inside the official app. Independent sign-in across vendor updates is still being verified in this preview.'],
 ['Does Hatrack work with Codex Desktop?','Yes. Each Codex profile gets its own CODEX_HOME, desktop state folder and file-based credentials. The ordinary ChatGPT desktop app and Codex CLI are not supported.'],
 ['Does it work with Claude Code or the Codex CLI?','No. Hatrack is for the desktop apps only. Command-line tools already support separate configuration folders.'],
 ['Does Hatrack see or copy my login?','No. You sign in inside the official desktop app. Hatrack does not copy credentials, has no account, and sends no telemetry.'],
 ['Is it free?','Yes. Hatrack is free and open source under the MIT licence.'],
 ['Is Hatrack made by Anthropic or OpenAI?','No. Hatrack is an independent project by Muneef Mumthas. Claude and Codex are trademarks of their owners.'],
];
---
<Layout faq={faq}><section class="hero wrap"><div class="hero-copy"><h1>Multiple Claude and Codex accounts.<br/><span>One Windows desktop.</span></h1><p class="lead">Hatrack gives each Claude Desktop and Codex Desktop account its own profile, data folder, shortcut and icon. Keep personal, work and client sessions apart and open the one you need.</p><div class="hero-actions"><a class="button" href={`${base}/download/`}>Get Hatrack for Windows<svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 4v12m-5-5 5 5 5-5M5 20h14"/></svg></a><a href={`${base}/guides/`}>See how it works →</a></div><p class="fine">Windows 11 x64 · Free &amp; open source · Preview build</p></div><figure class="product-stage"><img class="light-shot" src={`${base}/desktop.png`} width="1105" height="722" alt="Hatrack light theme listing separate Claude Desktop and Codex Desktop profiles with their own icons"/><img class="dark-shot" src={`${base}/desktop-dark.png`} width="1105" height="722" alt="Hatrack dark theme listing separate Claude Desktop and Codex Desktop profiles"/><figcaption>Actual Hatrack preview. Demonstration profiles; no signed-in accounts.</figcaption></figure></section>
<section class="app-section wrap"><div class="section-intro"><h2>Choose your app.<br/>Make the icon yours.</h2><p>Use the actual Claude or Codex logo in any colour, or upload an image. Check the taskbar preview before you create shortcuts.</p></div><figure class="app-shot"><img class="light-shot" src={`${base}/editor.png`} width="825" height="742" alt="Hatrack profile editor with the Claude logo, colour presets, image controls and taskbar previews" loading="lazy"/><img class="dark-shot" src={`${base}/editor-dark.png`} width="825" height="742" alt="Hatrack profile editor in dark mode" loading="lazy"/><figcaption>Actual preview interface with demonstration profiles. Authentication compatibility checks are still in progress.</figcaption></figure></section>
<section class="features wrap"><div><h2>Each profile.<br/>Its own local data.</h2><p class="lead compact">No Hatrack account. No cloud sync. No terminal setup.</p></div><dl><div><dt>Find what you already use</dt><dd>Automatic desktop-app detection, existing-profile discovery, and a manual location picker when you need it.</dd></div><div><dt>Choose a logo and colour</dt><dd>The recognisable Claude and Codex app logos, recoloured your way, or your own uploaded artwork. Preview it before creating shortcuts.</dd></div><div><dt>Keep local state separate</dt><dd>New profiles get separate data folders and Windows taskbar identities. Sign in within each official desktop app.</dd></div><div><dt>Keep control of your data</dt><dd>Removing a launcher preserves the profile folder. No credentials are copied and no profile data is uploaded.</dd></div></dl></section>
<section class="flow wrap"><h2>Install and create a profile.</h2><ol><li><strong>Install Hatrack</strong><p>One Windows installer. The runtime is included.</p></li><li><strong>Choose your desktop app</strong><p>Hatrack detects it. If it’s missing, follow the official download link.</p></li><li><strong>Create and open a profile</strong><p>Create your shortcuts and sign in inside the official app.</p></li></ol><aside><strong>For desktop apps, not CLI tools.</strong><p>Claude Desktop and Codex Desktop are the targets. This preview is awaiting independent authenticated-session acceptance; it is not a certified stable release.</p></aside></section>
<section class="faq wrap" aria-labelledby="faq-title"><h2 id="faq-title">Questions</h2><dl>{faq.map(([q,a])=><div><dt>{q}</dt><dd>{a}</dd></div>)}</dl></section>
<section class="closing wrap"><h2>Pick a hat.<br/>Open the account.</h2><div><a class="button" href={`${base}/download/`}>Get Hatrack</a><p>Independent software. Local profiles.<br/>MIT licensed. Yours to inspect and improve.</p></div></section></Layout>
